This article describes the development of hyphenation patterns and language support for Kazakh in \TeX{}. Approximately 106,000 words were extracted from an academic dictionary and processed to correct numerous encoding and typesetting errors. The Unicode-compatible \verb|pypatgen| utility was then used to generate hyphenation patterns, which were manually revised to account for the peculiarities of Kazakh syllabification. The resulting pattern dictionary is approximately 160 kilobytes in size and supports \pdfLaTeX{}, \XeLaTeX{}, and \LuaLaTeX{}. We also compare the new patterns with an earlier version available from \CTAN\ and demonstrate several cases in which our version produces more accurate hyphenation.
